DESCRIPTION:Register here\n\nSeptember 25 - 27\, 2026\n\nThis International Week of Deaf People\, MAP brings together a programme that celebrates Deaf culture\, Indian Sign Language (ISL)\, and the many ways we communicate\, create and share stories. Through workshops\, performances\, talks\, walkthroughs and playful activities\, the programme creates space for Deaf and hearing audiences to meet\, learn and make together. Led by Deaf artists\, facilitators and cultural practitioners\, these programmes invite us to experience the museum through visual language and new perspectives. At its heart\, the programme is about building a museum that feels more open\, welcoming and accessible to everyone.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nPlease find scheduled events as follows:\n\n 	Beyond Access: Rethinking Inclusion Through Art (Online panel discussion on Zoom)\n 	See through Sign\n 	Scavenger Hunt\n 	Visual Vernacular\n 	Stories Beyond Words: Comics in ISL\n 	Drawing in Signs\n 	Conservation Session\n 	Pottery Workshop\n 	Deaf Voices\, Real Stories: Breaking Barriers in India\n 	See Me\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nAccessibility Note: If you require accessibility support\, please write to access@map-india.org. MAP offers the accessibility services listed here—please refer to them. If you need any additional support beyond what’s mentioned\, do reach out to us.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCredits:Supported by Adobe Accessibility partners : Mphasis F1 Foundation Community partners: The Association of People with Disability\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
DTEND:20260927T093000Z
